# Search: alternative designs for a problem

You turn a problem (a context and its requirements) into two to four alternative designs, each a set of
choices for the decisions the problem raises, and write them as one rationale file that
`ddspace rationale check` accepts.
{% if space %}
The design space gives you the decisions (dimensions, `d:…`) and their alternatives (values, `v:…`). Name them
by id exactly as `ddspace query` prints them.
{% else %}
There is no design space: name each decision and option in your own words (`decision`, `option`).
{% endif %}
{% set ns = namespace(n=0) %}

## Steps

{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Requirements.** Read the problem and give each requirement an id: `R1`, `R2`, … for functional
   requirements, `Q1`, … for quality requirements (with the quality `attribute`, e.g. `durability`), `C1`, … for
   constraints. Keep the problem's own wording in `text`. Choose a short file id (lowercase, hyphens), `<id>`.
{% if space %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **The space.** Run `ddspace query info{{ where }}` (its `name` and `run` go in the file's `space`) and
   `ddspace query dimensions{{ where }}` to see the decisions.
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Search with single keywords.** `ddspace query search "<keyword>"{{ where }}` matches the whole query as one
   substring, so a phrase rarely matches: search one single keyword per call (`replication`, not
   `data replication strategy`), and try synonyms.
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Values and evidence.** For each relevant dimension run `ddspace query values "<d:id>"{{ where }}`, and for the
   values you may choose `ddspace query evidence "<v:id>"{{ where }}`: cite the passage ids (`doc`) it lists, with
   their stance.
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Relations.** Run `ddspace query relations --from "<d:id>"{{ where }}` for the dimensions you decide. Record a
   relation you rely on with its `source`, `target` and `type` as printed, and `holds` (whether it holds in this
   alternative).
{% endif %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Alternatives.** Build two to four alternatives that differ in the decisions that matter most for the
   requirements. Each alternative makes one choice per decision, with the requirement ids it serves (`drivers`)
   and a `reason`; lists in `considered` the options it weighed and set aside, and in `open` the decisions no
   requirement settles.
{% if space %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Check each alternative as a design point.** Run `ddspace point "<v:id>" "<v:id>" ... --no-llm{{ where }}` with the
   values that alternative chooses (leave its open dimensions out). Act on the warnings (two values of one
   dimension, a rejected value, a required dimension left out), and copy `attested_by` into the alternative's
   `point`.
{% endif %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Write the file** to `./rationale/<id>.json` (create the folder), in the shape below.
{% if space %}
   Write every id exactly as `ddspace query` prints them (`d:1`, `v:1.2`, `s01_p01`), never a label or slug.
{% endif %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Check until clean.** Run `ddspace rationale check rationale/<id>.json{{ where }}` and fix every error, then run
   it again, until `ok` is `true`. Each problem has a `code`, a JSON Pointer `path` into the file and often
   `candidates`: read them, they list what would fit (ids, passages, relations).
{% if space %}
   Set `space.graph_sha256` to the `graph_sha256` the check prints. Warnings: `unmet_requires` (add the
   required decision or say in `open` why it stays open), `graph_changed` (the space changed since you wrote
   the file: check the ids again).
{% endif %}
{% set ns.n = ns.n + 1 %}
{{ ns.n }}. **Present the alternatives.** Summarize them and the comparison for the user. In interactive use (not in a
{% if space %}
   study session), finish with `ddspace rationale build rationale/<id>.json{{ where }}`, which renders the file as a
   browsable explainer page in the wiki.
{% else %}
   study session), finish with `ddspace rationale build rationale/<id>.json --out .`, which renders the file as a
   browsable explainer page in `./explainers/` (with its assets).
{% endif %}

## Rules

- Never name a dimension, value or relation in prose that the file does not reference: what you say about the
  design must be in the file the check accepted.
- Requirement ids in `drivers` must be ids of `problem.requirements`.
- Do not change the file after the last clean check without checking it again.

## File shape

```json
{
  "schema": "ddspace-rationale/1",
  "id": "<id>",
  "mode": "search",
{% if space %}
  "space": {"workspace": "<name from ddspace query info>", "run": "<run from ddspace query info>", "graph_sha256": "<from ddspace rationale check>"},
{% else %}
  "space": null,
{% endif %}
  "problem": {
    "title": "<problem title>",
    "context": "<problem context>",
    "requirements": [
      {"id": "R1", "kind": "functional", "text": "<requirement>"},
      {"id": "Q1", "kind": "quality", "attribute": "<quality attribute>", "text": "<requirement>"},
      {"id": "C1", "kind": "constraint", "text": "<requirement>"}
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "<short name>",
      "summary": "<one or two sentences>",
      "choices": [
{% if space %}
        {"dimension_id": "d:1", "value_id": "v:1.1", "drivers": ["Q1"], "reason": "<why>",
         "evidence": [{"doc": "s01_p01", "stance": "accepts"}]}
{% else %}
        {"decision": "<decision>", "option": "<option>", "drivers": ["Q1"], "reason": "<why>"}
{% endif %}
      ],
      "considered": [
{% if space %}
        {"dimension_id": "d:1", "value_id": "v:1.2", "drivers": ["C1"], "reason": "<why not>"}
{% else %}
        {"decision": "<decision>", "option": "<another option>", "drivers": ["C1"], "reason": "<why not>"}
{% endif %}
      ],
      "open": [],
{% if space %}
      "relations": [
        {"source": "d:1", "target": "d:2", "type": "constrains", "holds": true, "note": "<what it means here>"}
      ],
      "point": {"attested_by": ["s:s1"]}
{% else %}
      "relations": []
{% endif %}
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "<short name>",
      "summary": "<one or two sentences>",
      "choices": [
{% if space %}
        {"dimension_id": "d:1", "value_id": "v:1.2", "drivers": ["C1"], "reason": "<why>"}
{% else %}
        {"decision": "<decision>", "option": "<another option>", "drivers": ["C1"], "reason": "<why>"}
{% endif %}
      ],
      "considered": [],
      "open": [
{% if space %}
        {"dimension_id": "d:2", "reason": "<why no requirement settles it>"}
{% else %}
        {"decision": "<another decision>", "reason": "<why no requirement settles it>"}
{% endif %}
      ],
      "relations": []
    }
  ],
  "comparison": [
{% if space %}
    {"dimension_id": "d:1", "note": "<how the alternatives differ on it>"}
{% else %}
    {"decision": "<decision>", "note": "<how the alternatives differ on it>"}
{% endif %}
  ],
  "uncovered": []
}
```
